 the assignee-update helper for the POST add operation. In that helper, repository issue/pull-request write permission is checked before assignee-name resolution and before the add-assignees mutation; failure returns HTTP 403. Under the declared condition that the principal lacks repository issue-write permission, the source therefore supports enforcement of the stated rejection-before-resolution-or-mutation policy. The authenticated issue-write token scope is distinct from the repository permission used by this control: the crop shows no token-scope decision, while it explicitly tests ctx.Repo.Permission.CanWriteIssuesOrPulls. The issue and requested user being present do not alter this ordering; user resolution is later than the permission check, and mutation is later still. This assessment is limited to the supplied entry and crop, not repository-wide completeness or deployment behavior.","facts":[{"id":"entry-post-issue-assignees","kind":"entry","statement":"The add-assignees API entry is the POST issue-assignees operation and invokes updateIssueAssignees with isAdd true.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":4,"endLine":6},{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":47,"endLine":49}]},{"id":"principal-context-doer","kind":"binding","statement":"The operation executes with the API context and later passes ctx.Doer to the assignee mutation service.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":53,"endLine":54},{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":80,"endLine":83}]},{"id":"resource-issue-by-repository-index","kind":"binding","statement":"The target issue is obtained using the repository ID and the path issue index before authorization proceeds.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":53,"endLine":58}]},{"id":"repository-permission-control","kind":"control","statement":"The helper checks repository permission to write issues or pull requests and returns HTTP 403 when the check fails.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":60,"endLine":63}]},{"id":"assignee-resolution-after-control","kind":"effect","statement":"Requested assignee names are resolved only after the repository permission check and its failure return.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":60,"endLine":63},{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":65,"endLine":75}]},{"id":"add-mutation-after-resolution","kind":"effect","statement":"The add-assignees service call occurs only after assignee IDs have been resolved and only on the add branch.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":70,"endLine":83}]},{"id":"nonwriter-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The decisive authorization condition in this path is the repository permission predicate, rather than any token-scope predicate shown in the supplied crop.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-46786967a1fedfdd","startLine":60,"endLine":63}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]}]}}],"tokens":{"input":2256,"output":1072,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":30888.424600000028,"stopReason":"tool_use"},"schemaValidation":{"valid":true,"diagnostics":[]},"endedAt":"2026-09-26T19:56:40.756Z"}}
